## What contradicts the goal (fix these first)

| Issue | Why it conflicts with What is F18? | Fix |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Stat **"18.6 Avg Age"** | The whole premise is "before 18." An average of 18.6 reads as "older than 18 on average" and quietly undermines the brand. | Remove it, or replace with **"Avg age at first record-break"** (which will be well under 18). |
| **"Get Featured" → Google Form** | The page says: *"There is no application process. You cannot apply your way in. You can only build your way in."* A "Get Featured" form is an application. | Rename to **"Submit a Tip"** or **"Nominate Someone"**, and reframe the form as third-party tips, not self-applications. |
| Three pillars: Discover / Verify / **Connect** ("VCs and schools can request introductions") | The stated goal is the opposite direction: F18 *pushes* a third-person letter to VCs and colleges so they chase the member. "Request an intro" makes it passive. | Replace with **Discover / Verify / Champion** (or "Advocate") — and explain that F18 *writes the case* and sends it. |
| No mention of the **VC letter / college letter** | This is the core differentiator vs. Forbes 30U30, YC directory, etc. It's missing from the landing page. | Add a fourth pillar or a hero sub-section: **"We don't just list them. We write the case for them."** |

