## The personal profile page → make it a "card"

Profiles today read like Wikipedia entries. A **card** should feel like something a VC partner could read in 60 seconds and forward to their team. The layout below maps 1:1 to the structure already defined in [What is F18?](https://www.notion.so/What-is-F18-35b9166fd9fd8094b05bd6a6bc990209?pvs=21) (Identity → What They Built → Verified Track Record → The Record They Broke → Targeted Letters).

### Proposed profile card structure

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  [Photo]   Name, Age, Country, Field                │
│            One-line record claim (the headline)     │
│            ──────────────────────────────────       │
│            "Youngest in [Country] to ship a [X]"    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

┌── What they built ──────────────────────────────────┐
│  2–3 sentence factual description. No marketing.    │
│  [link to product]  [link to demo]  [link to repo]  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

┌── Verified track record ────────────────────────────┐
│  • Funding raised:    $X (source)                   │
│  • Users:             X active (source)             │
│  • Press:             [Logo] [Logo] [Logo]          │
│  • Awards:            [Award] (year, source)        │
│  Every line links to a primary source.              │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

┌── The record ───────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Single sentence, constraint-bounded claim.         │
│  Why it holds up even without the age constraint.   │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

┌── For VCs ──────────────────┐  ┌── For Universities ┐
│  Third-person letter.       │  │  Third-person      │
│  ~150 words.                │  │  letter. ~150 words│
│  "You should be reaching    │  │                    │
│  out, not the other way."   │  │                    │
│  [Copy letter] [PDF]        │  │  [Copy] [PDF]      │
└─────────────────────────────┘  └────────────────────┘

[Share profile]   [Request intro through F18]
```

### Rules to enforce on every profile

- **One hero claim** at the top. If you can't write a single-sentence record, the person doesn't qualify yet.
- **Every metric is a hyperlink to a primary source.** This is the moat vs. Forbes / Fortune lists.
- **The two letters are visible by default**, not hidden behind a tab. They are the product.
- **Add a "Copy letter as PDF" button.** Members will literally send these to admissions / VCs — make it one click.
- **No comments, no follower counts, no social engagement widgets.** F18 is "not a social network" — the profile should look like a dossier, not a LinkedIn page.

